+- Moving a task to another project (`POST .../move`) needs the manager role in
+  the source project, like delete (else 403; checked first). The destination
+  must be readable by the user (else 404), must be a different project (else
+  400), must allow writes for the user (contributor or manager; else 403), and
+  must not be archived (else 409). The task keeps its ID, title, status and assignee, so the
+  assignee must be a contributor or manager of the destination (else 400).
+  A rejected move changes nothing.
 - Archived projects reject all writes with 409 (reads still work).
 - A task ID that does not belong to the project in the path → 404.
 
